# round007_exp012_localization_gate.sage
# EXP-012: build + validate the LOCALIZATION GATE on top of the round-005 first-fall meter.
#
# CAMPAIGN CONTEXT
# ----------------
# The base first-fall meter (Bardet-Faugere-Salvy nontrivial-syzygy meter on the
# HOMOGENEOUS leading-form system) reports d_ff = smallest degree D at which the
# homogeneous Macaulay map of the leading forms has a NONTRIVIAL (non-Koszul) kernel,
# and D_reg = the Froberg semi-regular degree of regularity. FIRES iff d_ff < D_reg.
#
# Round-6 finding (adjudicated): the base meter produces SPURIOUS fires. For the
# e-ring and power-sum m=3 Semaev systems the nontrivial syzygy was CONFINED to the
# factor-base-membership leading forms (which share the elementary-symmetric factor
# e1 -- the POS-A mechanism) while the SUMMATION POLYNOMIAL leading form contributed
# ZERO rows at the firing degree. Such a fire gives NO index-calculus solver leverage.
#
# THE GATE (this file). A fire is only MEANINGFUL if the firing syzygy actually
# INVOLVES the summation-polynomial leading form(s). meter_gated(...) computes, at the
# firing degree d_ff, whether the nontrivial (non-Koszul) kernel has nonzero support
# on the rows generated by the summation-poly leading forms.
#
# GATE_PASSES iff zeroing out the summation-poly row-block STRICTLY SHRINKS the
# nontrivial kernel at d_ff  <=> at least one nontrivial kernel vector has a nonzero
# coefficient on some monomial-multiple of a summation-poly leading form.
#
# This module LOADS the round-005 meter if available (to reuse its verified
# primitives) and otherwise falls back to inline re-implementations keyed to the
# SAME definitions, so the file parses and runs end-to-end on its own.
#
# Author: Algebra-System agent, EXP-012.

